// CBW Nutrition Worker v5 — regenerated 2026-07-27 from the authoritative FDA/INM export
// (FDA_Rounded_Export_for_INM_Crazy_Bowls__Wraps_07272026130429.xlsx). The FDA/INM export is now
// the SOURCE OF TRUTH for nutrition and allergen data on this menu, superseding the v3 Menu
// CMS + Nutritionix pipeline. Matching followed the reconciliation ledger
// (cbw-reconciliation-ledger.xlsx): Tab 1 "Confident Matches" (46 items, dataConfidence
// "verified") and Tab 2 "Alias - Needs Signoff" (8 of 9 items, dataConfidence "verified-alias";
// see exclusions below). No items were added or removed -- still exactly 76 items. The 36 new
// items present in the FDA export but absent from the live site are intentionally NOT included
// (separate opt-in decision, out of scope for this pass). The generic "Tacos" item was NOT
// restructured into the 9 individual FDA taco flavors (out of scope); it keeps its legacy numbers
// with dataConfidence "unverified-legacy".
//
// New fields added in v5:
//   - allergenFlags: per-item object of the 9 tracked allergens (milk, eggs, fish, shellfish,
//     treeNuts, peanuts, wheat, soy, sesame) as true/false/null -- machine-readable companion to
//     the existing human-readable `allergens` string. null means the source cell was blank.
//   - ingredientStatement: full ingredient statement text from the FDA export, or null if absent.
//   - dataConfidence: one of "verified" (Tab 1 match), "verified-alias" (Tab 2 match),
//     "unverified-legacy" (no FDA match, live calories > 0), "no-data" (no FDA match, live
//     calories == 0), or "phantom-unconfirmed" (BBQ Bowl, Buffalo Bowl, Caesar Bowl -- absent from
//     the official export entirely; their macros were copied long ago from the Wrap of the same
//     flavor and were never independently verified as real, distinct menu items).
//   - smallSize: for the 9 Bowls where the FDA export lists both "<Name> - Regular" and
//     "<Name> - Small" rows (Jerk, Fajita, Pesto, Power, Stir-Fry, Sweet & Sour, Teriyaki, Thai,
//     Mediterranean Bowl), the top-level nutrition fields hold the Regular-size row (matching the
//     single size/price the live site sells) and `smallSize` holds the Small row's
//     {calories, protein, carbs, fat, sodium, fiber, sugars, satFat, servingGrams}. This supersedes
//     the hardcoded small/regular lookup table that used to live in the site's React component.
//   - traceFields: when the FDA export reports a value as the text "<1" (trace amount), it is
//     stored here as the number 0 and the affected field name is recorded in this array so the UI
//     can render "trace" instead of a bare zero if desired. Never emit the literal string "<1" in a
//     numeric field.
//   - duplicateOf: set on the "Chips" item (-> "bag-of-chips") because the live site independently
//     lists both "Chips" and "Bag of Chips", and both map to the single FDA "Bag of Chips" row.
//     Both live items are kept as-is; de-duplication is a client decision, not made here.
//
// ALIAS CORRECTION: the ledger's Tab 2 proposed live "Vegetable Wontons" -> FDA
// "Vegetable Wontons - 3 Piece", but that undercounts by 100 calories. Live shows 340 cal / 7g
// protein / 41g carb, which is an exact match for FDA "Vegetable Wontons - 5 Piece" instead --
// that is the row actually used here, with dataConfidence "verified-alias".
//
// dietaryTags is deliberately left null for every item, exactly as in v3 -- NOT populated by this
// pass. The FDA export's "Contains Meat" and "Contains Animal Products" columns are 100% empty for
// all 89 items, so vegan/vegetarian status cannot be derived from this source. Populating
// dietaryTags requires an independent, human-verified source and explicit sign-off.
//
// ALLERGEN SAFETY NOTE -- READ BEFORE TRUSTING A "false"/"N" ON ANY WRAP: the FDA export's wrap
// item rows (BBQ/Breakfast/Buffalo/Caesar/Jerk/Mediterranean/Pesto/Power/Thai Wrap, etc.) exclude
// the tortilla itself -- their ingredient statements list only the filling, and most show
// Wheat=N/false despite being served in a wheat flour tortilla. A wrap's Wheat=false (or its
// allergens string omitting Wheat) reflects only the filling and must NEVER be read or displayed
// as "gluten-free" or "wheat-free" for the assembled item. (Lettuce Wrap items are the
// gluten-free/tortilla-free format and are a separate menu line.)
//
// Preserved verbatim from v3: DISCLAIMER text, CORS headers, and the export default fetch handler
// below (including its literal "generated"/"source" strings, which describe the v3 pipeline and
// were intentionally left untouched per this regeneration's scope).
// Regenerate by re-running this file's build script against a fresh FDA/INM export + updated
// reconciliation ledger. Do not hand-edit MENU_DATA.

// dietaryTags: populated for 8 items ONLY. Seven were verified by reading their full
// FDA ingredient statement and screening for meat, dairy, egg and honey — the three
// edamame, Carrots, Broccoli w/ Olive Oil & Herb and Mixed Veggies (vegan+vegetarian),
// plus GF Quinoa Falafel (vegetarian only; its tzatziki contains yogurt). The eighth,
// Banana, has NO row in the FDA export at all (hence dataConfidence unverified-legacy
// on its nutrition) and is tagged vegan on the self-evident grounds that it is a whole
// piece of fruit — the diet tag and the nutrition provenance are independent here. Every other item is deliberately null pending sign-off from CBW: the source
// export's "Contains Meat" and "Contains Animal Products" columns are 100% empty and
// meat is not an allergen, so nothing else can be justified from this data.
// The site's React component treats a null dietaryTags as NOT vegan by design — it no
// longer guesses from ingredient keywords, because every composed item is built with
// Grilled Chicken by default and the ingredient text never names that default protein.
// This 8-item set intentionally matches the published JSON-LD payload so the
// machine-readable claims and the on-page filter cannot disagree.

// AS-SERVED WHEAT CORRECTION: the source export's Wraps rows are filling-only and
// omit the tortilla, so 8 wraps arrived flagged Wheat=N despite being served in a
// wheat tortilla. All three tortillas CBW carries (Flour, Tomato, Whole Wheat) are
// Wheat=Y in the modifiers export, so Wheat has been added to those 8 items and
// marked wheatFromTortilla:true. Without this, a celiac guest filtering Gluten-Free
// was shown BBQ/Buffalo/Caesar/Jerk/Mediterranean/Pesto/Power/Thai Wrap. Lettuce
// Wraps are excluded (romaine, not tortilla) and so are 'tortilla on the side' items
// (Breakfast Bowl, Fajita Bowl) where the tortilla is a decline-able component.
// The 10 corrected items: BBQ/Buffalo/Caesar/Jerk/Mediterranean/Pesto/Power/Thai Wrap
// plus Breakfast Wrap and Healthy Burrito (both wrapped in a tortilla despite sitting
// in the Breakfast category).

